{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And these are the sons of Zibeon: Aiah and Anah.</b> Its sense is 'Aiah and Anah,' for the waw is superfluous; like it (2 Samuel 15:34): ״עבד אביך ואני מאז״ — whose sense is 'I have been your father's servant from aforetime.' And Scripture declares that Anah was the son of Zibeon. Earlier it mentioned that Zibeon and Anah were brothers, sons of Seir, and so that you not say that the Anah mentioned there is this one's uncle, therefore Scripture states: ״הוא ענה אשר מצא את הימים״ — 'he is the Anah who found the yemim.' And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: he is 'the Anah from aforetime' (דמעיקרא), because Zibeon lay with his mother and begot from her Anah. And the reason Scripture counted him among the sons of Seir is that everyone thought of him as a son of Seir; but Scripture declares to us the truth, that he is 'from aforetime' and is not a son of Seir but rather a son of Zibeon — he is his son and he is his brother. Therefore Scripture cries out: 'he is the Anah who found the yemim in the wilderness' — he is the flaw that brought flaws into the world, for he devised in his thought the species of mules, that is, what issues from the crossbreeding of one species with one not of its kind, such as one who mates a horse with a she-ass or a donkey with a mare, and a mule issues from between them; and this was reckoned to him as wisdom in that generation. And according to the view of Onkelos, who translated 'mighty men' (גבריא), the yemim would be like Emim (אימים), and the plain sense of Scripture would be that men from the nation called Emim came against this Anah — formerly a great and tall people like the Anakim — and sought to steal from him the donkeys of Zibeon his father, and he was in the wilderness with none to help him, yet he delivered them from their hand. And therefore it says: 'he is the Anah' renowned for this act of valor. Thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:02.497123278Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}